      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"The Anaconda development container currently includes a version of the Pillow imaging library that is known to contain a security weakness. Users of the container need assurance that the image they pull does not expose them to this risk. The required behavior is that the container image is built with a Pillow version that is at least 10.3.0, which contains the necessary patches. When the container is started, any command that queries the installed Pillow version should report 10.3.0 or newer. Additionally, the container's validation script must verify this version requirement as part of its suite of package checks, failing the test suite if the version is lower than the minimum.\n\nTo achieve this, the Docker build process for the Anaconda devcontainer must be modified so that the package manager installs Pillow at version 10.3.0 (or a later version if available). The build script that runs after the base image is pulled should explicitly request this version, ensuring that the upgrade supersedes any older version that may be present in the upstream base image. The validation script that runs after the container is built should include a check that confirms the installed Pillow version matches the minimum required version. This check should be performed in the same manner as other package version assertions in the script, and the overall test outcome should reflect success only when the version constraint is satisfied.\n\nThe change must be transparent to end users: they should not need to modify their configuration or run additional commands to obtain the safe version of Pillow. The container should work out‑of‑the‑box with the updated package, and the test suite should pass without manual intervention, providing confidence that the security issue has been mitigated.\"\n",
          "id": "prt_ef940227f001cL6994jIihdb49",
          "sessionID": "ses_106bfddbdffednan8x93CTGUw3",
          "messageID": "msg_ef940227e0014wMGGszFI5lZG6"
        }
      ]
